+## Acceptance-suite failures (10, browser-only)
+
+An external Cypress suite against the real DOM reports 10 failures. Root cause: `render()`
+in `js/app.js` calls `todoList.innerHTML = ''` then rebuilds every `<li>` from scratch on every
+state change, destroying all DOM node references. The happy-dom harness re-queries after each
+step and masks the defect; a real browser holds pre-action references and sees them detached.
+
+### Failure groups
+
+**1-2 (Toggle all):** `toggleAllTodos()` → state change → `render()` → list rebuilt. Cypress
+`cy.eq()` references the detached element.
+
+**3-4 (Toggle individual):** Same pattern: toggle click handler calls `render()`, list rebuilt.
+
+**5-10 (Editing):** `dblclick` handler sets `todo.editing = true`, calls `render()`. But
+`render()` re-reads from localStorage via `getTodos()`, and `setTodos()` strips the `editing`
+property before persisting. So `todo.editing` is lost, the `editing` class is never added to the
+new `<li>`, and the `.edit` input stays `display: none` per TodoMVC CSS. Additionally, the old
+`li` reference is used after `render()`, operating on a detached node.
+
+### Fix direction
+
+Preserve element identity: mutate the existing `<li>` in place (toggle `.completed` class,
+show/hide `.edit` input) instead of calling `render()` to rebuild the list. The `render()`
+function already re-reads from localStorage — eliminate that re-read and use the in-memory
+`todos` array for rendering, or skip re-rendering entirely for single-item mutations.
+
+### Scenarios added
+
+- `todo-management.feature` Rule: DOM identity preservation (2 scenarios)
+- `todo-management.feature` Rule: Editing visibility (2 scenarios)
+
+These 4 scenarios are in `watchbill.json`.
+
